## Proxy Protocol v2 Header Format
```
Signature (12 bytes):     0x0D, 0x0A, 0x0D, 0x0A, 0x00, 0x0D, 0x0A, 0x51, 0x55, 
0x49, 0x54, 0x0A
Version/Command (1 byte): 0x21 (PROXY command, version 2)
Family (1 byte):          0x11 (TCP over IPv4)
Address Length (2 bytes): Big-endian uint16 (minimum 12 for TCP4)
Source IP (4 bytes):      IPv4 address
Dest IP (4 bytes):        IPv4 address
Source Port (2 bytes):    Big-endian uint16
Dest Port (2 bytes):      Big-endian uint16
Optional TLV:             Additional data (skipped if present)
```

## Compatibility
- Maintains full backward compatibility with Proxy Protocol v1
- Supports AWS NLB and other modern load balancers using Proxy Protocol v2
- Properly handles both text-based (v1) and binary (v2) formats
